    "rationale": "The design exhibits a critical authority laundering risk (TC7) where untrusted vendor quotes dictate irreversible payments executed by a downstream peer agent. Behavioral prompt instructions reduce immediate likelihood but leave the residual risk high, as they are fully dependent on model compliance. Upgrading the model or increasing autonomy will bypass the instructions, restoring the critical risk profile. Protocol security is also weak due to unpinned agent cards and shared static token trust."
